[/center]

[center][i]Built to work the way AAF intends, with thanks to [b]Dagobaking[/b], author of AAF, for his technical guidance. Our notes on AAF are [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport/issues/1]reviewed by him[/url], and his word is final.[/i][/center]

[center][size=4][b][url=https://pixeldrain.com/u/7ZnoDbUt]▶ Watch the demo[/url][/b][/size] (1:16, the Third Rail: voiced lines, subtitles, bystanders)[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[center][b]The Commonwealth family: made to work together[/b]
[b]Rapport[/b] (this page): runs the scenes · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109225]Chemistry[/url]: NPCs find each other · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109433]Overture[/url]: you talk someone into it · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url]: working genitals, arousal and contact · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url]: the physics behind them · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109439]Silhouette[/url]: everyone gets a body of their own · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/fallout4/collections/dmt85e]Ivy's Panties[/url]: all of it, installed for you[/center]

[center][size=4][b]New here? [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6679]The setup guide[/url]: from the body to the scenes, in one order, with what to take and what to skip.[/b][/size][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]In short[/color][/b][/size]

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Characters talk to each other during a scene, in real voices, with subtitles and lip sync.[/*]
[*]Faces fit what is happening, and the two look at each other.[/*]
[*]Bystanders notice the scene and sometimes speak.[/*]
[*]Everyone remembers who they were with, and has their own character: orientation and persona.[/*]
[*]A narrator explains who is involved, why, and shows the score.[/*]
[*]Nobody ends a scene left naked.[/*]
[*]A free camera in every scene you're in, back to your own view when it ends.[/*]
[/list][b]What you need[/b]: F4SE, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/31304]AAF[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url], LooksMenu, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url] and the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url].
[b]How it goes[/b]: install with Vortex or MO2. The installer checks your setup first. Then add an addon that starts scenes. Details: [b]Before you play[/b], below.

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Rapport runs the scene. It does not start one.[/b] AAF plays the animations; Rapport runs everything around them. Addons decide [i]when[/i] a scene begins: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109225]Chemistry[/url] lets NPCs find each other, and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109433]Overture[/url] lets you walk up to someone and try your luck. Rapport alone starts nothing. It is built for AAF (a Fallout 4 mod that plays animations), as an F4SE framework (F4SE is the Fallout 4 script extender).

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/family.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]What you get[/color][/b][/size]

[center][size=4][b]Moans timed to each stroke Anatomy's physics measures, in each NPC's own voice and temperament.[/b][/size][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/moans.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Scene moans.[/b] 419 takes, 2 voices × 4 temperaments; painful pleasure for the receiver, a climax that lands. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6668]Scenes and pairing →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/wardrobe.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Nobody left naked.[/b] AAF puts clothes back on only when a scene ends cleanly. Rapport keeps its own snapshot of what they wore, saved in your save, and puts back whatever is missing. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/identity.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Change who they are.[/b] Face anyone and press a hotkey to set their orientation or persona, for this save only. Every mod in the family follows. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6669]Relationships and people →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/glances.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Faces that fit the act, and eye contact.[/b] Animation packs give faces to 0.4% of actions; Rapport picks a face for 99.2%. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/voices-map.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Every character speaks.[/b] 6,656 recordings. 629 voice types were analysed, so a unique character borrows the closest-sounding voice. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/narrator.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]The Narrator.[/b] It says who is involved and why, and shows the score, part by part. All four moments are on by default. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6670]The Narrator →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1151/images/109219/109219-1791392392-947607543.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]A free camera.[/b] In every AAF scene you are in, Rapport takes the camera over from AAF at the first animation: fly it and look around with your keys and mouse while the world keeps running. When the scene ends, your first- or third-person view comes back. FreeCamera = 0 in Rapport.ini turns it off.[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Everything else, one line each[/color][/b][/size]

[b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6668]Scenes and pairing →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]It reads the whole animation tree, from the scene asked for to a real ending.[/*]
[*]A 600 s stop: no scene runs forever.[/*]
[*]Same-sex pairs prefer their own animations, never an empty scene.[/*]
[*]Never anyone unconscious, restrained or frozen; nothing before Vault 111.[/*]
[*]Rapport never picks a scene that needs a Servitron's mouth: she has none. She can still receive, and use her hands and body.[/*]
[/list][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]Faces nothing can close: Anatomy's hook acts after the engine's merge.[/*]
[*]Real dialogue with lip sync; every take checked against its subtitle.[/*]
[*]Aftermath in game hours, on the receiver: 4 by default, 1-48 on the MCM.[/*]
[*]No holstered pistol during sex, with Visible Favorites.[/*]
[/list][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6669]Relationships and people →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]A bond from −1 to +1 between everyone who touched, starting from the game's own ranks.[/*]
[*]Four kinds of people, spread evenly and stable forever.[/*]
[*]Bystanders notice: one roll per scene, about 1 in 3 speak.[/*]
[/list][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6672]Under the hood, and for mod authors →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]It cannot crash your game through the script engine: Papyrus asks, C++ answers.[/*]
[*]At most one AAF call per poll: other mods' scripts never stall.[/*]
[*]Refusals are told apart from starts: no phantom scenes, no frozen NPCs.[/*]
[*]0.004-0.028 ms a pass for 49-78 actors: zero script lag.[/*]
[*]Addon door, ApiVersion 205, and our notes on AAF for any author.[/*]
[/list][center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Open source, and built in public[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Source:[/b] [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport]github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport[/url], GPL-3.0, all of it. Every commit is built on a clean [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport/actions]GitHub Actions[/url] runner, which publishes the DLL's SHA256 in a log nobody can edit afterwards.[/*]
[*][b]Honest about the build:[/b] the DLL in the download is built on our machine, with a different compiler toolset than the public build, so their hashes differ. The public build proves the source compiles; it cannot prove your download exactly, byte for byte.[/*]
[*][b]Scanned:[/b] the VirusTotal badge above is generated from the scan result and names the build it is about.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Before you play[/color][/b][/size]

[quote]
[b]Install with Vortex or MO2; installing by hand is not supported.[/b] The installer refuses to run without AAF, LooksMenu and Anatomy. [b]Required:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url] and the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url] 1.2.3: Rapport's faces, moans and body sounds run through them. [b]Optional:[/b] MCM, Commonwealth Moisturizer for the aftermath, Visible Favorites for the holster hiding. Upgrading from 0.2.4 mid-save is safe.

[b]Don't fast travel in the ~10 seconds while two NPCs walk to each other to start a scene[/b] (fixed in AAF 1.7.8; the public AAF is still 1.7.4.1). Once the scene has started, fast travel is safe. The crash is inside AAF's interface while the area unloads; a mod gets no warning that a fast travel is coming, and no distance setting removes the window.

[b]Nothing starts until you leave Vault 111.[/b] No scene and no approach during the game's opening, from character creation to the vault door; alternate starts and MS Skip Prewar Sanctuary work as expected. Using an unusual alternate start that never finishes the opening? MCM, first page, [i]Start now[/i].

[b]Old-gen or Anniversary Edition.[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 with F4SE 0.6.23, or the Anniversary Edition 1.11.x with F4SE 0.7.9. Both need [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url]: without it the game stops at launch. Every class Rapport reads is checked before use, and on a mismatch Rapport turns itself off for that session and Rapport.log names it. [b]Downgraded from next-gen?[/b] Every F4SE plugin needs its old-gen build too: AAF first (Rapport needs it), then Buffout 4, Address Library, LooksMenu, Dialogue Menu Fix and the rest. A crash at launch after a downgrade is one of those or the downgrade itself, never Rapport. f4se.log lists the plugins as they load.

[b]Uninstalling?[/b] Set [font=Courier New]PanicClear=1[/font] in [font=Courier New]Data/F4SE/Plugins/Rapport.ini[/font] and load your save once first. It removes everything Rapport applied, faces and aftermath included. Nothing Rapport applies is something only Rapport can remove.[/quote][size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Incompatibilities[/color][/b][/size]

Known conflicts, from real reports and the code. Found another one? Tell us in the Bugs tab.
[list]
[*][b]CumOverlays[/b]: its overlays would stack with Rapport's aftermath. Rapport turns them off during its own scenes, and Commonwealth Moisturizer is the only aftermath backend. Keep CumOverlays if you want it for other mods, but expect nothing from it in Rapport scenes.[/*]
[*][b]Original OCBPC (not the Anatomy Engine)[/b]: Rapport needs the Anatomy Engine's cbp.dll, and tells you once a session if it didn't start.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/107225]Commonwealth Camera[/url]'s Camera Lag[/b]: incompatible with the free camera. With Camera Lag on, the mouse can't turn the camera; turn Camera Lag off in Commonwealth Camera's settings.[/*]
[*]Nothing else known.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Do I need AAF?[/b]
[spoiler]Yes. AAF is the mod that plays the animations, and Rapport runs the scene around them. The installer refuses to run without it.[/spoiler]

[b]Will scenes start by themselves?[/b]
[spoiler]No. Rapport starts nothing: NPC scenes come from Chemistry and approaches from Overture. Install one of them, or both.[/spoiler]

[b]Does it replace other mods?[/b]
[spoiler]AAF Sex 'Em Up and AAF Autonomy Enhanced do the same job, so if either is installed Rapport stops their quests, never deleting anything, and logs why. Commonwealth Moisturizer's own scene listener is stopped the same way while Rapport drives the aftermath. Everything else AAF plays keeps working, and Rapport adds its faces and aftermath to those scenes too.[/spoiler]

[b]Where do I report what I see?[/b]
[spoiler]The Bugs tab, with Rapport.log. Every report gets read.[/spoiler]

[b]Where is the full list of features and settings?[/b]
[spoiler]In the five articles on the Articles tab: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6668]Scenes and pairing[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces voices and bodies[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6669]Relationships and people[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6670]The Narrator[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6672]Under the hood and for mod authors[/url]. Every MCM and Rapport.ini setting is in the sticky posts.[/spoiler]

[b]Can I stop scenes from starting?[/b]
[spoiler]Rapport starts nothing by itself: NPC scenes come from Chemistry and approaches from Overture, so turn those off (or uninstall them). Rapport keeps scoring and reporting to Rapport.log.[/spoiler]

